From: USA-RedDragon <USA-RedDragon@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 07:09:17 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] fix(compression): one classifier for the user's words

The task snapshot and the verbatim user-message section used two prefix lists that drifted apart: the snapshot took a subagent result ([ASYNC DELEGATION ...]) as the user's request, and both quoted peer-agent messages ([Agent message ...]) as the user's words, which crowded real messages out of the verbatim budget. One classifier in conversation_compression_scaffolding now serves the snapshot, the verbatim section, the auto-focus hint, anchor restoration and the recall query, and the summarizer input labels such rows USER ROLE, NOT WRITTEN BY THE USER instead of USER. It also drops recalled memory from quotes, unwraps steer messages, skips gateway notices and leading system notes, and keeps hub page answers whole up to 16K chars instead of cutting them at 4K. Bug fix, no key.
